  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.3.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.3.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "1. When Adrian had built a palace, and wished to dedicate it by that wicked ceremonial, and began to seek responses by sacrifices to idols, and to the demons that dwell in idols, they replied, and said:",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.3.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.3.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "“The widow Symphorosa, with her seven sons, wounds us day by day in invoking her God.",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.3.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.3.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "If she therefore, together with her sons, shall offer sacrifice, we promise to make good all that you ask.”",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.3.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.3.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Then Adrian ordered her to be seized, along with her sons, and advised them in courteous terms to consent to offer sacrifice to the idols.",
    "chunk_index": 23,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.3.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.3.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "To him, however, the blessed Symphorosa answered: “My husband Getulius, together with his brother Amantius, when they were tribunes in thy service,",
    "chunk_index": 24,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.3.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.3.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "suffered different punishments for the name of Christ, rather than consent to sacrifice to idols, and, like good athletes, they overcame thy demons in death.",
    "chunk_index": 25,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.3.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.3.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For, rather than be prevailed on, they chose to be beheaded, and suffered death:",
    "chunk_index": 26,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.3.s8",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.3.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "which death, being endured for the name of Christ, gained them temporal ignominy indeed among men of this earth, but everlasting honour and glory among the angels;",
    "chunk_index": 27,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.3.s9",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.3.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and moving now among them, and exhibiting trophies of their sufferings, they enjoy eternal life with the King eternal in the heavens.”",
    "chunk_index": 28,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.4.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.4.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "2. The Emperor Adrian said to the holy Symphorosa: “Either sacrifice thou along with thy sons to the omnipotent gods, or else I shall cause thee to be sacrificed thyself, together with thy sons.”",
    "chunk_index": 29,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.4.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.4.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The blessed Symphorosa answered: “And whence is this great good to me, that I should be deemed worthy along with my sons to be offered as an oblation to God?”",
    "chunk_index": 30,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.4.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.4.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The Emperor Adrian said: “I shall cause thee to be sacrificed to my gods.” The blessed Symphorosa replied:",
    "chunk_index": 31,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.4.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.4.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "“Thy gods cannot take me in sacrifice; but if I am burned for the name of Christ, my God, I shall rather consume those demons of thine.”",
    "chunk_index": 32,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.4.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.4.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The Emperor Adrian said: “Choose thou one of these alternatives: either sacrifice to my gods, or perish by an evil death.”",
    "chunk_index": 33,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.4.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.4.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The blessed Symphorosa replied: “Thou thinkest that my mind can be altered by some kind of terror; whereas I long to rest with my husband Getulius, whom thou didst put to death for Christ’s name.”",
    "chunk_index": 34,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      300,
      600
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa#PassSymph.4.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/passion-of-symphorosa",
    "canonical_ref": "PassSymph.4.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Then the Emperor Adrian ordered her to be led away to the temple of Hercules, and there first to be beaten with blows on the cheek, and afterwards to be suspended by the hair.",
